# Offline and Sync

Client-side offline behavior per [`.cursor/api-contract.mdc`](../../.cursor/api-contract.mdc).

## Mandatory rules

- Connectivity is a hint, not proof of reachability.
- Must queue offline drafts and pending writes in structured local storage when required.
- Sync operations should be idempotent where possible.
- Must show sync states: pending, syncing, synced, failed, conflict.
- Must not silently discard offline changes.
- Conflict handling must be explicit; surface `409` with version metadata.
- Repositories must expose consistent local and remote views.
- After successful HTTP writes, controllers must reconcile via `WorkspaceSyncEngine` (safe typed deltas or the smallest HTTP refresh); widgets must never consume raw websocket payloads.

## Online-only (never queue)

Auth/session changes, entitlement/break-glass approval, payments/refunds, mortuary release, final closeout — see `api-contract.mdc`.

## Sync queue fields

| Field | Purpose |
|---|---|
| local id | stable local reference |
| operation type | create, update, delete, upload |
| payload | serialized request |
| status | pending, syncing, failed, synced, conflict |
| retry count | retry policy |
| timestamps | ordering and diagnostics |

